# netsurf: Vita browsing -- controls, home page, URL entry, cookies
# Generated 2026-09-24
#
# README §14.8's v0 chrome: a URL, a page, back/forward on the buttons,
# bookmarks in a text file on ux0:; §14.6's URL entry without the OSK.
# - vita/input.c/.h (new): touch (tap = click, drag = scroll; the front
#   panel's 1920x1088 halved), a left-stick pointer with CROSS to click
#   (press down, click up, hover tracked), right stick and D-pad scroll,
#   L/R back/forward, SQUARE zoom 100/125/150/200 %, TRIANGLE text entry,
#   START home. Input is a per-pass record, from the pad or from a script.
# - vita/chrome.c/.h (new): home page generated at start-up from
#   ux0:data/VitaBrowser/bookmarks.txt ("Title | URL", written with
#   defaults if missing) plus the test pages; typed text -> URL (a URL as
#   is, a host gets https:// (an IPv4 address or localhost http://), words
#   search lite.duckduckgo.com); text goes
#   into the focused field when there is one (key presses), else opens as
#   a URL; the system keyboard (sceImeDialog, URL mode) on the Vita,
#   VITA_SIM_TYPE in the simulator.
# - vita/remote.c/.h (new): a LAN listener on :8080 served from the main
#   loop, never blocking it: GET / is a form, /open?url= opens the URL on
#   the Vita, /cookie sets and shows a cookie (the jar's persistence test).
#   The simulator moves the port (VITA_SIM_REMOTE_PORT).
# - vita/interact.c/.h (new): the autotest's interaction pass, after pass
#   N: 22 scripted steps through vita_input_browse() on the IN-* test pages
#   (taps, pointer, back/forward, drag, zoom, blocked hosts, a form filled
#   in and sent, typed URL, a URL pushed to the listener over loopback, the
#   cookie jar saved, home), each checked and logged; dumps IN-zoom125,
#   IN-block, IN-form-sent.
# - main.c: the test functions move behind SELECT (SELECT + SQUARE
#   autotest, + CIRCLE dump, + TRIANGLE memory probe, + L/R test pages,
#   + START quit); the cookie jar loaded at start-up and saved after page
#   loads (at most every 10 s) and on quit, since the PS button runs no
#   exit code; start page = the home page (argv[1] overrides: the
#   simulator); the HUD shows title/URL/loading on top and zoom, blocked
#   count and the listener's address below; the pointer is drawn.
# - window.c/.h: the title kept for the HUD; the throbber and title
#   repaint it. Makefile: the new sources, -lSceTouch_stub.
#   Makefile.defaults: NETSURF_VITA_START_PAGE = the home page.
# See docs/phase-0/10-hardware-test-plan.md §Run 14.

